course: dictionary
lesson: 8515
title: Satisfied: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have several meanings. The words around it show you which meaning the writer wants. The most common meaning is pleased, because you got what you wanted or needed. «She was satisfied with her score.» She is happy with the score she got.
explain: Satisfied can also mean sure that something is true. «I am satisfied that he is telling the truth» means you have good reasons to believe him. It can mean having had enough too: «The food satisfied our hunger» means we were no longer hungry.
explain: In maths, a number satisfies an equation when it makes the equation true. Check by putting the number back in. For example, x = 3 satisfies x + 2 = 5, because 3 + 2 = 5 is true.
fact: «Satisfied» means pleased because you got what you wanted or needed.
fact: «Satisfied» can mean sure that something is true, as in «be satisfied that».
fact: «Satisfied» can mean having had enough, as in «The food satisfied our hunger».
fact: In maths, «x = 3 satisfies x + 2 = 5», because 3 + 2 = 5 is true.
fact: «Dissatisfied» means not pleased. It has two s's because dis + satisfied keeps both letters.
exercise: «She was satisfied with her score.» What does satisfied mean here? | Angry and shouting | *Pleased with what she got | Very tired after a long run | Lost in the park
exercise: «The food satisfied our hunger.» What does satisfied mean here? | Pleased with the shop | Sure that something is true | Angry about the price | *Had enough, so we were no longer hungry
exercise: In maths, does x = 4 satisfy x + 2 = 5? | Yes, because 4 + 2 = 5 | Yes, because 4 is bigger than 2 | Maybe, it depends on the sign | *No, because 4 + 2 is 6, not 5
test: «I am satisfied that he is telling the truth.» What does satisfied mean here? | Hungry | *Sure that something is true | Pleased with a present | Finished eating
test: Which number satisfies x + 5 = 9? | 5 | *4 | 3 | 14
exam: Which word has two s's, the same as dissatisfied? | *misspell | legal | appear | disappear
